<p dir="auto">This PR primarily adds the "Brief history of hash-based SPA routing" section to the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Router" rel="nofollow">Router</a> glossary page.</p>
<p dir="auto">Other changes are minor edits for formatting, punctuation, and clarity on the "Router" and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/History_API/Working_with_the_History_API" rel="nofollow">Working with the History API</a> pages.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">We were missing historical context for hash routing. The new section informs developers why <code class="notranslate">#/</code> and <code class="notranslate">#!/</code> routing practices came about, why they are obsolete now, and what to use instead.</p>
<p dir="auto">/cc <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/tantek/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/tantek">@tantek</a></p>]]></content>
